                <pb facs="0756" n="676" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg676"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terres to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-12-16"><hi rendition="#italic">December 16,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Terres reports the arrival of General Nord on December 16; that great
                    excitement prevails; that shooting is going on in the city; that serious trouble
                    is expected; that the Haitian secretary of the interior, with general police, is
                    at the United States legation.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
